      "label": "Theft as a cost is mapped onto the masked individual",
      "description": "The text 'after theft' explicitly maps the concept of theft (a criminal act) onto the masked individual in the visual material. The meme uses this mapping to satirically imply that the thief is responsible for the additional $1.37, creating an absurd juxtaposition between a criminal act and a financial transaction. The masked individual is visually represented as the entity that 'causes' the cost increase, even though in reality theft is not a financial transaction.",
